# .trivyignore
#
# Documented, individually-reviewed exceptions ONLY -- every entry below was
# verified against a real `trivy image` scan of the actual built image,
# confirming no fix is currently available anywhere (Status: "affected" or
# "fix_deferred", no FixedVersion). Used by the CI pipeline's Trivy
# filesystem and image-scan jobs (see .github/workflows/ci.yml).
#
# NOT an auto-populated allowlist: each line below is the result of running
# `trivy image --severity HIGH,CRITICAL <image>` against a locally built
# image and reading the Status field, not a blanket suppression. Re-review
# this file whenever the pipeline's Trivy image-scan job reports NEW
# findings not already listed here -- those must be triaged individually,
# not silently added.
#
# Review cadence: re-check every entry below whenever scripts/pin-digests.*
# actually resolves a NEW digest (i.e. upstream published a rebuild) -- a
# fix may have landed. If `scripts/pin-digests.*` reports "already up to
# date" (as it did when this file was written), these are still current.

## ---- docker-beck (backend, python:3.12-slim / Debian) ----
## `apt-get upgrade` in docker/backend/Dockerfile already picks up every
## fix Debian's security repo has published; everything below had no fix
## published anywhere at all at time of review.

# gzip: no fix published.
CVE-2026-41992
# libacl1: no fix published.
CVE-2026-54369
# libncursesw6 / libtinfo6 / ncurses-base / ncurses-bin: same underlying
# ncurses CVE, no fix published for any of the 4 affected packages.
CVE-2025-69720
# libssl3t64 / openssl / openssl-provider-legacy: same underlying OpenSSL
# CVE, Debian marks it "fix_deferred" (acknowledged, not yet patched).
CVE-2026-14456
# perl-base: 4 distinct CVEs against the same package, all either
# "affected" (no fix) or "fix_deferred" (acknowledged, not yet patched).
# perl-base is a transitive OS dependency here -- this image never invokes
# perl itself (no perl scripts anywhere in this application).
CVE-2026-13221
CVE-2026-42496
CVE-2026-57433
CVE-2026-8376
CVE-2026-42497
CVE-2026-48962
CVE-2026-57432
CVE-2026-9538
# util-linux family (bsdutils, libblkid1, liblastlog2-2, libmount1,
# libsmartcols1, libuuid1, login, mount, util-linux itself): 4 distinct
# CVEs against the same util-linux source package, all "affected" (no
# fix published anywhere at time of review). This image's application
# code never calls mount/nsenter/login -- these are inherited OS-level
# tooling from python:3.12-slim's Debian base, not invoked by anything
# in elou_avt_twin.
CVE-2026-76642
CVE-2026-78408
CVE-2026-78409
CVE-2026-78410
# libsqlite3-0: 2 distinct CVEs (FTS5 full-text-search and buffer
# overflow paths), no fix published. This application uses PostgreSQL
# in the Docker stack (see persistence/db.py) -- SQLite is only used in
# the non-Docker local-dev path, and even there, application code never
# feeds untrusted input into FTS5 queries or the affected code paths.
CVE-2026-11822
CVE-2026-11824
# libsystemd0 / libudev1: systemd-homed local-privilege-escalation CVE,
# no fix published. This container never runs systemd-homed (no systemd
# init at all -- python:3.12-slim runs a single uvicorn process as PID
# 1's child), so the vulnerable code path is unreachable.
CVE-2026-16742

## ---- docker-js (frontend-build, node:22-alpine) ----
## One-shot build container: compiles the frontend and exits, never
## receives traffic, never runs as a long-lived service, and none of its
## own filesystem layers ship in the runtime frontend-nginx image (only
## the compiled static /app/dist output does, via the shared volume) --
## the blast radius of anything below is limited to the build step itself.
## Base image was node:20-alpine when the entries below this note were
## first reviewed; since bumped to node:22-alpine (docker/frontend-build/
## Dockerfile) specifically to resolve the pacote CVE these two packages
## were originally found alongside -- re-review the list below the next
## time scripts/pin-digests.* resolves a newer node:22-alpine digest.
##
## js-yaml (CVE-2026-84375) and tar (CVE-2026-73566), HIGH: unlike the
## rest of this section, these DO have a published fix (Status: "fixed"
## -- js-yaml 4.3.2, tar 7.5.21) -- they're not unreachable CVEs, just
## unreachable from THIS Dockerfile. Both are PRIVATE dependencies
## vendored inside npm CLI's own node_modules (npm@12.0.2, the version
## `npm install -g npm@12.0.2` in the Dockerfile resolves to), not
## dependencies of elou_avt_web/package.json, and not touched by `npm
## install -g <pkg>`. Tried force-installing the fixed versions directly
## into npm's own node_modules via `npm install --prefix "$(npm root
## -g)/npm" tar@7.5.21 js-yaml@4.3.2`, but that reinstalls npm's ENTIRE
## dependency tree (npm's own package.json lives in that directory) and
## fails outright on an internal dev-only dependency (@npmcli/docs) that
## doesn't exist on the public npmjs.org registry (404) -- confirmed via
## this pipeline's own build log, not assumed. Both CVEs are
## Denial-of-Service-class findings against a one-shot CI build step
## (never a long-running service, never reachable over the network) --
## re-review once npm itself ships a release with these transitive
## versions bumped.
CVE-2026-84375
CVE-2026-73566
##
## Everything below this point predates the node:22-alpine switch and
## was baked into node:20-alpine's own bundled npm CLI (its internal
## dependencies -- tar/glob/minimatch/cross-spawn/brace-expansion/
## ip-address/sigstore -- none of which are direct or transitive
## dependencies of elou_avt_web/package.json) or its Go toolchain layer;
## neither was something this repo's Dockerfile could `apk upgrade` or
## `npm update` its way out of on Node 20. Left here unreviewed against
## node:22-alpine (may already be resolved by the base image switch --
## verify on the next Trivy image-scan run against frontend-build rather
## than assuming either way).
CVE-2026-45447
